#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-move — move the Claude desktop app's Code session list to another account.

When you sign the Claude desktop app into a different account, the Code tab's session list
looks empty: the list is stored per account, under
  ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude-code-sessions/<account>/<org>/local_*.json
while the transcripts themselves live in ~/.claude/projects and are not tied to any account.
This tool copies those list entries from one account to another. It never deletes anything,
and it backs up the target account's list before it writes.

Unofficial; not affiliated with or endorsed by Anthropic. It relies on the desktop app's
on-disk layout, which can change in any release.

Usage:
  claude-move list
  claude-move sessions <account>
  claude-move name <account> <label>
  claude-move to <target> [--from <source>] [--days N] [--all] [--only TEXT] [--dry-run]
  claude-move undo [--list] [--backup NAME] [--dry-run]
  claude-move import-cli [--config DIR] [--project PATH] [--session ID ...] [--days N] [--dry-run]
  claude-move usage [--refresh] [--html] [--config DIR ...]
  claude-move panel [--port N] [--idle SECONDS]
  claude-move app install|uninstall [--dir DIR] [--no-dock] [--icon IMAGE]
  claude-move watch install|uninstall
<account> is a label you gave with `name`, or the first characters of the account id.
"""
